hadiths[133]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1201","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj informed me, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: the rich are invited to it, and the poor are barred from it; and whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"1202","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Kaysan al-Yashkuri narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah: that a man wanted to marry a woman of the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Look at her, for in the eyes of the women of the Ansar there is something. Al-Humaydi said: Meaning smallness."
"1203","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has pardoned my ummah for what their hearts whisper, so long as they do not act upon it or speak of it."
"1204","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sulayman ibn Dawud swore and said: I shall go around tonight to seventy wives, each of them bringing a boy who fights in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. His companion — or the angel — said to him: Say, if Allah wills. But he forgot, so he went around to seventy wives, and none of them brought anything except one, who brought half a boy. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he said, if Allah wills, he would not have broken his oath, and it would have been a means to attaining his need."
"1205","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hujayr al-Taymi narrated to us, from Tawus, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"1206","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar? He said: Spend it on yourself. He said: I have another. He said: Spend it on your child. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have another. He said: Spend it on your family. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have another. He said: Spend it on your servant. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have another. He said: You know best. Sa'id said: Then Abu Hurayrah, when he narrated this hadith, would say: Your child says: Spend on me, to whom will you leave me? Your wife says: Spend on me or divorce me; your servant says: Spend on me or sell me."
"1207","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Imran ibn Zibyan narrated to us, from a man of Banu Hanifah, that he heard him saying: Abu Hurayrah said: Do you know Rajjal? I said: Yes. He said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: His molar tooth in the Fire will be greater than Uhud. He had accepted Islam, then apostatized and joined Musaylimah. And he said: Two rams butted, and the dearer to me is that my ram prevails."
"1208","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Are you harmed in seeing the sun at noon when there is no cloud? They said: No. He said: Are you harmed in seeing the moon on the night of full moon when there is no cloud? They said: No. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you will not be harmed in seeing your Lord except as you are harmed in seeing one of them. Then He meets the servant and says: O so-and-so, did I not honour you, make you a leader, marry you, subject for you horses and camels, and leave you to lead and take a fourth? He says: Yes indeed, my Lord. He says: Did you think you would meet Me? He says: No. He says: So I forget you as you forgot Me. Then He meets the second and says the like, and he answers the like. Then He meets the third, who says: I believed in You, Your Book, and Your Messenger; I prayed, fasted, and gave charity, and he praises goodness as much as he can. He says: Then here it is. Then He says: Shall We not send Our witness against you? So he thinks to himself: Who will testify against me? Then his mouth is sealed, and it is said to his thigh: Speak, so his thigh, flesh, and bones speak of his deeds as they were; and that is to establish proof from himself. That is the hypocrite, and that is the one with whom Allah the Exalted is angry. Then a caller calls: Let every nation follow what it used to worship besides Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; so the devils and crosses and their patrons follow to Hell. He said: And we remain, we the believers. Then our Lord comes to us, and He is our Lord, and He rewards us, and says: Why are these here? They say: We are the believing servants of Allah; we believed in Allah and associate nothing with Him; this is our station until our Lord comes to us, and He is our Lord, and He rewards us. He said: Then He proceeds until He comes to the Bridge, upon which are hooks of fire that snatch people; at that point intercession is permitted — O Allah, grant safety, O Allah, grant safety. When they cross the Bridge, then whoever spent a pair of what his right hand possessed of wealth in the path of Allah, every keeper of Paradise calls him: O servant of Allah, O Muslim, this is good, so come. He said: Then Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed this servant suffers no loss: he leaves no gate but enters through another. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with his hand, then said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, indeed I hope you are among them."
"1209","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zinad narrated to us, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will come while two men trade a garment, neither completing the sale nor folding it."
"1210","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: One who heard Abu Hurayrah informed me, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it. And recite if you wish: And extended shade. And the dawn prayer is attended by the angels of the night and the angels of the day. And recite if you wish: And the recitation of dawn; indeed, the recitation of dawn is witnessed."
"1211","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and the prayer is established, begin with supper. Sufyan said: And I heard no one saying 'when supper is served' except al-Zuhri."
"1212","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old. My mothers would urge me to serve him. He entered our house, and we milked for him from a domestic sheep of ours, and it was mixed with water from a well in the house. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, with Abu Bakr on his left and a Bedouin on his right, and 'Umar at a side. 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, give to Abu Bakr. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to the Bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"1213","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sever ties, do not turn away from one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another; and be servants of Allah, brothers. And it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days. It was said to Sufyan: Nor engage in najsh? He said: No."
"1214","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Wa'il ibn Dawud narrated to us, from his son Bakr ibn Wa'il, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for Safiyyah with sawiq and dates. Sufyan said: And I heard al-Zuhri narrating it but I did not retain it; and Bakr ibn Wa'il used to sit with al-Zuhri along with us."
"1215","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not make nabidh in gourds or pitched vessels."
"1216","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three follow the dead to his grave: his family, his wealth, and his deeds; two return and one remains: his family and wealth return, and his deeds remain."
"1217","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Qasim the traveller narrated to us in the year one hundred and twenty, when I was thirteen years, four months, and a half old, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a ruin belonging to Banu al-Najjar, intending to relieve himself, and he came out alarmed — or he said frightened — saying: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, to let you hear of the punishment of the people of the graves what He has let me hear."
"1218","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The last look I cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was when he lifted the curtain on Monday, while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr. When they saw him, they stirred as it were, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) signalled to them to stay firm. I looked at his face as though it were a page of a mushaf. He let down the curtain, and he died at the end of that day (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1219","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse and his right side was grazed, so we entered to visit him. The prayer came, and he prayed with us sitting, and we prayed behind him sitting. When he finished his prayer, he said: The imam is made only to be followed: when he says the takbir, say the takbir; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he says 'Allah hears him who praises Him,' say: O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise; when he prostrates, prostrate; and when he prays sitting, pray all sitting."
"1220","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the Hour. He said: What have you prepared for it? He did not mention much except that he said: I love Allah and His Messenger. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are with the one you love. Abu 'Ali said: I heard al-Humaydi saying: Ibn 'Uyaynah met eighty-six of the Tabi'in, and he used to say: I have not seen the like of Ayyub. Al-Humaydi said: Sufyan said: And the wording of al-Zuhri, when he narrated to us from Anas and Sahl, was: I heard, I heard."
"1221","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Zuhr at Madinah as four, and I prayed with him 'Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two."
"1222","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to the same effect as the preceding narration."
"1223","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I prayed Zuhr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Medina, four rak'ahs, and I prayed Asr with him at Dhu al-Hulayfah, two rak'ahs."
"1224","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I prayed, along with an orphan boy, behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in our house, with my mother Umm Sulaym behind us."
"1225","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, having heard it from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invited the Ansar in order to grant them lands in Bahrain, but they said: Not until you grant our Muhajir brothers the same. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will see selfish preference after me, so be patient until you meet me."
"1226","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque and the people began staring at him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped them and said: Pour a bucket of water over it."
"1227","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best houses of the Ansar are the house of Banu al-Najjar, then the house of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the house of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then the house of Banu Sa'idah. And he said: In all the houses of the Ansar there is good."
"1228","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon Khaybar early on a Thursday morning; they had opened the fortress and come out of it with their spades, and when they saw him they rushed back into the fortress, saying: Muhammad and the army. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, and he raised his hands: Khaybar is ruined; when we descend into the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned."
"1229","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman used to open the recitation with Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"1230","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khaybar, we found donkeys outside the village and slaughtered them and cooked some of them, whereupon the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced: Indeed Allah and His Messenger forbid you from it, for it is filth from the work of Satan. So the pots were overturned with what was in them while they were boiling."
"1231","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the people took a valley and the Ansar took a mountain pass, I would take the mountain pass of the Ansar; and were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar. The Ansar are my inner store and my trust, so be good to those of them who do good, and overlook those of them who do wrong. Ibn Jud'an said: And al-Hasan added to it for me: Except in a prescribed hadd punishment."
"1232","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Abu Talhah used to scatter his quiver before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), kneeling on his knees and saying: My face is a shield for your face, and my soul a ransom for your soul. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a company of men. Anas said: And I saw Ibn Umm Maktum carrying the banner of the Muslims in one of their battles."
"1233","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Ukaydir of Dumah gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a cloak as a gift, and the people marvelled at its beauty, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than it."
"1234","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jud'an narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: Intercession was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whereupon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I will take hold of the ring of Paradise and rattle it."
"1235","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between the Muhajirun and the Ansar in our house. It was said to him: Did not the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no alliance in Islam? So Anas repeated it and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood in our house between the Muhajirun and the Ansar. Sufyan said: The scholars explained it: He established alliance means he made them brothers."
"1236","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Dabbi narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Miqsam al-Dabbi, from his father, from Shu'bah ibn al-Taw'am, who said: Qays ibn Asim asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about alliances, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no alliance in Islam, but hold fast to the alliances of the pre-Islamic era."
"1237","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieve over an expedition as he grieved over the companions of Bi'r Ma'unah when they were killed; and they used to be called the Reciters."
"1238","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi said: The first thing we heard from him, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he invoked blessings upon one of them but did not invoke blessings upon the other, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, you invoked blessings upon him but did not invoke blessings upon me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one praised Allah, while you did not praise Him."
"1239","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his servant: Gently, drive slowly with the glass vessels, meaning the women."
"1240","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I was standing serving some uncles of mine among the Ansar, pouring date-wine for them, when a man came to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in alarm. We said: What is the matter? He said: Wine has been prohibited. So they said to me: Pour it out, Anas. So I poured it out. Al-Nadr ibn Anas said: That was their wine on that day."
"1241","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: We set out in the morning on this day with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Mina to Arafah; some of us proclaimed the takbir and some of us proclaimed the talbiyah, and none of us criticized the others for it."
"1242","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca in the year of the Conquest with a helmet on his head."
"1243","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picking out the pumpkin from the dish, and I have loved it ever since."
"1244","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah asking Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wear a ring? He said: Yes; it is as if I am looking at its shine on his hand on a moonlit night."
"1245","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I was riding behind Abu Talhah, saying: Here I am, with a Hajj and an Umrah together."
"1246","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Sulaym, the registrar of Banu Zuhrah, narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to this narration."
"1247","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped; a slave belonging to an Ansari clan called Banu Bayadah, named Abu Taybah, cupped him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him a sa' or two sa's, or a mudd or two mudds, and he spoke to his masters, so they reduced his tax, meaning his levy."
"1248","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina, the people cast lots for dwellings, and the lot of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf fell upon Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'. Sa'd said to him: Come, I will share my wealth with you, and I will give up for you whichever of my two wives you wish, and I will spare you work. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to him: May Allah bless your family and your wealth for you; show me the market. So he went out and earned something, then proposed to a woman and married her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: For how much did you marry her? He said: For a date-stone's weight of gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"1249","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw some phlegm in the direction of prayer in the mosque and scraped it off, then turned to the people in anger and said: Would one of you like to be spat in the face? Then he said: When a servant stands in prayer he is facing his Lord, so let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot; and if something comes up suddenly, let him put it in his garment and fold it like this. And al-Humaydi pointed to the edge of his garment and rubbed it."
"1250","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan al-Qardusi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Jamrah and slaughtered his sacrifice, he handed his right side to the barber, who shaved it, then handed him his left side, which he shaved, then he handed it to Abu Talhah and ordered him to distribute it among the people."
"1251","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Dates were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he began distributing them while sitting hurriedly, eating quickly and eagerly."
"1252","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar and Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, that they heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A man granted freedom to a slave boy of his after his death, owning no other property, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold him, and Nu'aym ibn al-Nahham bought him. Amr ibn Dinar said: Jabir said: A Coptic slave who died in the first year of the rule of Ibn al-Zubayr. Abu al-Zubayr added: His name was Ya'qub the Copt."
"1253","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar and Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, that they heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A man entered the mosque while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing on the pulpit delivering the sermon on Friday, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Have you prayed? He said: No. He said: Then pray two rak'ahs. Sufyan said: In his narration Abu al-Zubayr named the man Sulayk ibn Amr al-Ghatafani."
"1254","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ja'dah narrated to us, he said: I saw al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan enter the mosque of Wasit on Friday while Ibn Hubayrah was delivering the sermon on the pulpit, and he prayed two rak'ahs then sat down."
"1255","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us and said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: On the day of al-Hudaybiyah we were one thousand four hundred, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Today you are the best of the people of the earth. Jabir said: Had I my sight, I would have shown you the place of the tree."
"1256","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Jubayr ibn Shaybah narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far al-Makhzumi saying: I said to Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari while he was circumambulating the House: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid fasting on Friday? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this House."
"1257","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Have you married, Jabir? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a previously married woman? I said: A previously married woman. He said: Why not a young girl whom you would play with and who would play with you? I said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was killed on the day of Uhud leaving nine daughters, so they became nine sisters to me, and I did not wish to bring together with them a foolish young girl like them, but rather a woman who would comb their hair and look after them. He said: You did right."
"1258","Sufyan said: Then I met Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir and he narrated it to me, adding a word which Amr did not say. He said: I heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me when I married: Jabir, have you taken cushions? I said: O Messenger of Allah, whence would we have cushions? He said: Indeed, they will come to be."
"1259","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked for anything at all and said: No."
"1260","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: I fell ill, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr visited me on foot; I lost consciousness, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, performed ablution, then poured it over me, and I came to. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how should I settle my wealth? What should I do with my wealth? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent until the verse of inheritance was revealed."
"1261","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The verse of inheritance was revealed concerning me. Abu Bakr said: Sufyan did not hear it from Abu al-Zubayr."
"1262","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people on the day of the Trench, and al-Zubayr volunteered; then he called them again and al-Zubayr volunteered; then he called them again and al-Zubayr volunteered, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr. And Sufyan said: Hisham ibn Urwah added: And the son of my maternal aunt."
"1263","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A boy was born in the quarter and his father named him al-Qasim, so we said to his father: We will not call you Abu al-Qasim, nor will we please your eye with it. So his father came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Name your son Abd al-Rahman."
"1264","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali informed me, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Jabir, when the wealth of Bahrain comes, I will give you like this and like this and like this. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away before the wealth of Bahrain came, and it came during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, so Abu Bakr ordered a caller who announced: Whoever has a debt owed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or a promise, let him come. Jabir said: So I came to Abu Bakr and said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the wealth of Bahrain comes, I will give you like this and like this and like this. So Abu Bakr scooped out for me once, then said to me: Count it. I counted it and found it to be five hundred, and he said: Take the like of it twice more."
"1265","Sufyan said: Then I heard Ibn al-Munkadir narrating that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying the same, except that he said: So he scooped out for me three times. And Ibn al-Munkadir added: Jabir said: Then I came to Abu Bakr afterwards and said to him: Give me, but he did not give me; then I came to him and said: Give me, but he did not give me; then I came to him and said: Give me, but he did not give me, so I said: O Abu Bakr, I asked you to give me and you did not give me, then I asked you to give me and you did not give me, so either give me or be miserly toward me. He said: You said: Be miserly toward me? And what disease is worse than miserliness? Every time I withheld from you it was only while intending to give you."
"1266","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded licking the fingers and licking the dish. He said: And he said: One does not know in which part of it the blessing lies."
"1267","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us; I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a palace, or a house, and I said: Whose is this? It was said: It belongs to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Were it not for your jealousy, O Abu Hafs, I would have entered it. He said: So Umar wept and said: Would one be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?"
"1268","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a palace, or a house, and I heard a noise in it, and I said: Whose is this? It was said: It belongs to a man of Quraysh, and I hoped that I was he, but it was said: It belongs to Umar ibn al-Khattab. Were it not for your jealousy, O Abu Hafs, I would have entered it. He said: So Umar wept and said: Would one be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?"
"1269","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit."
"1270","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar said: Khuda'ah, while the people of Medina say khada'ah."
"1271","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a campaign when a man of the Muhajirun kicked a man of the Ansar, so the Ansari said: O Ansar! And the Muhajir said: O Muhajirun! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard it and said: What is this? They said: A man of the Muhajirun kicked a man of the Ansar; the Ansari said: O Ansar, and the Muhajir said: O Muhajirun. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with this call of the pre-Islamic era? Leave it, for it is foul. Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul said: Have they done it? By Allah, if we return to Medina the mightiest will surely expel the humblest from it. Jabir said: The Ansar in Medina were more numerous than the Muhajirun when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, then the Muhajirun increased afterwards. He said: So Umar said: Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, lest the people talk that Muhammad kills his companions."
"1272","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Harun al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul said to his father: By Allah, you shall never enter Medina until you say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the mightiest and I am the humblest. He said: And he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, it has reached me that you intend to kill my father; by the One Who sent you with the truth, I have never looked at his face out of awe of him, and if you wish that I bring you his head, I will bring it to you, for I dislike seeing the killer of my father."
"1273","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A Bedouin came to Medina and pledged allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to emigrate, then he developed a fever and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, release me from my pledge. He said: No. When the fever grew severe he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, release me from my pledge. He said: No. Then the fever grew severe and he went out fleeing from Medina, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Medina is like the bellows; it expels its dross and purifies its good."
"1274","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us with three hundred riders, our commander being Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, to intercept a caravan of Quraysh; severe hunger struck us until we ate tree leaves, and that army was called the Army of Leaves. He said: The sea cast out for us, while we were on the coast, a creature called the ambergris fish; we ate from it for half a month, used it as condiment and anointed ourselves with its fat until our bodies recovered. He said: Abu Ubaydah took one of its ribs and set it up, then looked for the tallest man and the greatest camel in the army and ordered him to mount the camel then pass beneath it, and he did so and passed beneath it. Then we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Do you have any of it with you? We said: No."
"1275","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to the same effect, with the addition: There was among us a man with a bag containing dates; he would give us a handful from it, then it came down to a single date, and when it was exhausted we felt its loss."
"1276","Abu Bakr al-Humaydi said: Sufyan did not hear it from Abu al-Zubayr. He said: Amr narrated to us, from Jabir, that he heard him saying: There was among us a man, and when hunger grew severe he slaughtered three camels, then he slaughtered three camels, then he slaughtered three camels, then Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah forbade him."
"1277","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr informed us, from Abu Salih, from Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah, who said: I said to my father: I was in the army, the Army of Leaves, and hunger struck the people, so my father said to me: Slaughter. I said: I slaughtered. Then severe hunger struck them and my father said to me: Slaughter. I said: I slaughtered. Then severe hunger struck them and my father said to me: Slaughter. Then my father said: Slaughter. I said: I was forbidden."
"1278","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah pointing to his two ears: I testify that I heard with these two ears of mine the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some people will come out of the Fire and enter Paradise."
"1279","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr, yours if Allah wills, narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: Mu'adh ibn Jabal used to pray Isha with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then return and lead his people in it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed Isha one night. He said: So Mu'adh prayed it with him, then returned and led his people, opening with Surah al-Baqarah, whereupon a man behind him stepped aside, prayed alone, then left. They said to him: You have turned hypocrite. He said: No, but I shall go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him. So he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, you delayed Isha last night, and Mu'adh prayed it with you, then returned and led us, opening with Surah al-Baqarah; when I saw that, I stepped back and prayed alone, for we are people of water-camels, working with our hands. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Mu'adh and said: Are you a causer of trial, Mu'adh? Are you a causer of trial? Recite such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah, and he listed the surahs. Sufyan said: And Abu al-Zubayr added in it that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; By the night when it covers; By the sky containing great stars; By the sun and its brightness; By the sky and the night-comer. Sufyan said: So I said to Amr ibn Dinar: Abu al-Zubayr says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; By the night when it covers; By the sun and its brightness; By the sky and the night-comer; By the sky containing great stars. Amr said: It is this, or something like this."
"1280","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul after he had been placed in his grave. He said: So he ordered that he be brought out, placed him upon his knees, clothed him with his shirt, and breathed upon him some of his saliva, and Allah knows best."
"1281","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu Harun Musa ibn Abi Isa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayy said to him, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two shirts on: Clothe him, O Messenger of Allah, with the shirt that touches your skin."
"1282","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if I fight in the cause of Allah until I am killed, where shall I be? He said: In Paradise. He said: So he threw down some dates that were in his hand, then fought until he was killed."
"1283","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will deal with Ka'b ibn al-Ashraf? He has harmed Allah and His Messenger. Muhammad ibn Maslamah said: O Messenger of Allah, would you like me to kill him? He said: Yes. He said: Then permit me. So he permitted him, and Muhammad ibn Maslamah went to Ka'b and said: This man has demanded charity from us and burdened us, and I have come to borrow from you. He said: And what is more, by Allah, you will surely grow weary of him. Muhammad ibn Maslamah said: We have followed him and we dislike leaving him until we see how his affair turns out. He said: Pledge me something. He said: What shall I pledge you? He said: Pledge me your sons? Muhammad said to him: The son of one of us would be insulted, it being said of him: Pledged for two loads of dates. He said: Then your women. He said: You are the most handsome of the Arabs; shall we pledge you our women? Rather we shall pledge you weapons. He said: Yes, and he promised to come to him. He said: They were four; Amr named two of them: Muhammad ibn Maslamah and Abu Na'ilah. They came to him while he was wrapped, with the scent of perfume wafting from him. They said: We have never smelled a scent as pleasant as tonight's. He said: I have with me such-and-such woman, the most perfumed of the Arabs. Muhammad said: Permit me to smell. He said: Smell. Then he said: Permit me to return. He said: So he returned, seized his head, and said: Strike him. So they struck him until they killed him."
"1284","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Al-Ubayshi narrated to us, from Ikrimah, who said: His wife said to him: I hear a sound in which I smell blood. He said: It is only Abu Na'ilah, my brother; had he found me asleep he would not have woken me, and the generous man, if called to a lance thrust, would answer it. And those who came to him were named: Muhammad ibn Maslamah, Abu Na'ilah, Abbad ibn Bishr, Abu Abs ibn Jabr, and al-Harith ibn Mu'adh."
"1285","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: Did you hear Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man who passed with arrows in the mosque: Hold their blades? He said: Yes."
"1286","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr informed us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: Concerning us, Banu Harithah and Banu Salimah, was revealed: When two parties among you were about to lose heart, and I would not love that it had not been revealed, because of the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: And Allah was their Protector."
"1287","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed us horse meat and forbade us donkey meat."
"1288","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sharecropping. Sufyan said: Everything I heard from Amr ibn Dinar in which he said to us: I heard Jabir, except these two narrations, meaning horse meat and sharecropping, I do not know whether there is someone between him and Jabir in them or not; as for the narration of the arrows, I myself said to him: Did you hear Jabir? According to what I narrated to you."
"1289","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Yasar informed us: Tariq was governor, and he judged that the life-grant goes to the heir, on the authority of the saying of Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1290","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We used to practise withdrawal while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us and the Qur'an was being revealed."
"1291","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Iyad, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, brother of Banu Salimah: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a slave girl and I practise withdrawal from her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That will not prevent anything which Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has decreed. He said: The man went away and had hardly stayed but a short while when he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you know that that slave girl has become pregnant? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger."
"1292","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: When there was revealed: Say: He is Able to send punishment upon you from above you, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or from beneath your feet, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek refuge in Your Face. Or confuse you as sects and make some of you taste the violence of others, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These two are lighter, or these two are easier."
"1293","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: We used to carry the meat of sacrificial animals as provision to Medina in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1294","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: My father was killed on the day of Uhud and was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed before him, having been mutilated; I wanted to uncover him but my people forbade me, and I wanted to uncover him while my people forbade me, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that he be lifted. Then he heard the voice of a weeping woman and said: Who is this? They said: The daughter of Amr, or the sister of Amr. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not weep, or why does she weep? The angels, peace be upon them, kept shading him with their wings until he was lifted. Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Munkadir always used to doubt in this narration."
"1295","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn al-Munkadir saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Jews used to say: Whoever comes to his wife from behind in her front, the child will come cross-eyed, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish."
"1296","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour three handfuls of water over his head while in a state of major impurity."
"1297","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Jabir, do you know that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brought your father back to life and said to him: Wish. He said: That I be brought back to life and killed in Your cause once more. So He said: I have decreed that they shall not return."
"1298","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to me, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a woman of the Ansar, who spread for him a mat of hers, the mat being clustered palm trees, and slaughtered a sheep for him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from it. Then the time of Zuhr came, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, performed ablution, then prayed Zuhr. Then the remainder of the sheep was brought and he ate from it, then stood for Asr without performing ablution. Then I came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said to his family: Do you have anything? They said: No. He said: Then where is your milking ewe? So it was brought and he milked it and made for us colostrum from it; he ate from it and we ate. Then he stood for prayer and prayed without performing ablution. Then I came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and two handfuls were brought; one was placed before him and the other behind him. He ate and we ate, then he prayed without performing ablution."
"1299","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House and prayed two rak'ahs behind the Station, he returned to the Stone and touched it, then went out to al-Safa and said: We begin with what Allah began with: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah."
"1300","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: When the feet of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended into the valley, he hastened until he had crossed the valley."
"1301","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered one hundred camels as sacrifice; Ali, peace be upon him, came from Yemen and he made him a partner in his camels in a third; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered sixty-six camels, and ordered Ali, who slaughtered thirty-four. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a piece from every slaughtered camel, which was cooked, and they ate of the meat and sipped of the broth. Sufyan said: The people of Arabic say: And they sipped."
"1302","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A townsman shall not sell for a desert-dweller; leave the people, Allah providing for some of them through others."
"1303","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was distributing the spoils of Hunayn at al-Ji'ranah, with unminted gold in the lap of Bilal, when a man came to him and said: O Muhammad, be just, for you have not been just. He said: Woe to you, who will be just if I am not just? Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for he has companions, or is among companions, who recite the Qur'an without it passing their throats; they pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the game."
"1304","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, more than once or twice, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you has land or palm trees, let him not sell it until he has offered it to his partner. Sufyan said: The Kufans used to come to Abu al-Zubayr asking him about this narration, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated it to us on your authority."
"1305","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep your children in at the darkness of Isha, and beware of staying up talking after people have settled to rest, for you do not know what Allah sends forth of His creation; so close the doors, extinguish the lamps, overturn the vessels, and tie the waterskins."
"1306","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us: That he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who plants a crop from which a human, jinn, bird, wild animal, beast, riding animal, or anything eats, except that it shall be charity for him."
"1307","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: We did not pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to die, but we pledged to him that we would not flee."
"1308","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best prayer is that with long standing, the best jihad is that of one whose blood is shed and whose horse is hamstrung, and the best charity is the effort of one of little means, or what is given out of sufficiency."
"1309","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the people to the pledge, he found a man among us called al-Jadd ibn Qays hiding beneath the belly of his camel."
"1310","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah, when asked about garlic, saying: There was no garlic in our land on that day; what was forbidden was only onions and leeks."
"1311","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned remitting losses from calamities in some manner. Sufyan said: I do not remember it except that he mentioned its remission, and I do not remember how much that remission was."
"1312","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Qays narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to the same effect."
"1313","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Qays narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Atiq, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of years in advance."
"1314","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet, to the same effect."
"1315","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: Nabidh used to be made for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a waterskin, and if they did not find a waterskin, then in a stone basin."
"1316","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the earnings of the cupper: Feed it to the water-carrying camel."
"1317","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he caught up with me while I was upon a water-carrying camel of ours that seemed slow, so I said: O the grief of my mother! We always have a bad water-camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prodded it with a stick he had, or a hooked staff, and I saw it such that hardly anything went ahead of it."
"1318","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream as if my neck was struck. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why does one of you narrate Satan's playing with him?"
"1319","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid me my due and gave me extra."
"1320","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir, who said: It was announced among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended the Hajj, and Medina filled up; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the season of Hajj and at the time of Hajj, and when he overlooked al-Bayda he raised his voice in talbiyah from it, and the people raised theirs with him."
"1321","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Medina fasting until, when he was at Kura' al-Ghamim, he raised a vessel, placed it upon his palm while upon his mount, held back those ahead of him until those behind him caught up, then drank while the people looked at him. Afterwards it reached him that some people had fasted, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those are the disobedient."
"1322","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not practise ruqba nor umra; whoever is granted something by ruqba or umra, it follows the course of inheritance."
"1323","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that he said: When the Negus died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Today a righteous servant has died, so stand and pray over Ashamah."
"1324","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah, muhaqalah and mukhabarah, and that dates not be sold until their soundness is evident, and that they not be sold except for dinars or dirhams, though he permitted arayas. Mukhabarah is leasing land for a third or a quarter; muhaqalah is selling standing grain for wheat; muzabanah is selling fruit on the tree for picked dates."
"1325","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: We arrived at Mecca on the morning of the fourth, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I known beforehand what I know now, I would not have done what I did. He said: And he ordered his companions to dissolve their ihram, so they said: What kind of dissolution? He said: Complete dissolution; the Umrah has entered into the Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."
"1326","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: A man of the people of Fadak committed adultery, so the people of Fadak wrote to some Jews in Medina: Ask Muhammad about that; if he orders you with flogging, take it from him, and if he orders you with stoning, do not take it from him. So they asked him about that, and he said: Send to me your two most learned men. They brought a one-eyed man called Ibn Suriya, and another. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Are you the most learned among those behind you? They said: Our people have set us apart for that. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Is not the Torah with you, containing the judgment of Allah, the Exalted? They said: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I adjure you by the One Who split the sea for the Children of Israel, shaded you with clouds, saved you from the people of Pharaoh, and sent down manna and quails upon the Children of Israel: What do you find in the Torah concerning stoning? One of them said to the other: I have never been adjured with the like of this. Then they said: We find repeated looking to be adultery, embracing to be adultery, and kissing to be adultery, but when four testify that they saw him going in and out as the kohl-stick enters the kohl-container, stoning becomes obligatory. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is it. So he ordered concerning him and he was stoned, and there was revealed: If they come to you, judge between them or turn away from them; if you turn away from them they will not harm you at all, but if you judge, judge between them with justice, to the end of the verse."
"1327","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, concerning the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Listeners to falsehood, being the Jews of Medina; listeners on behalf of other people, being the people of Fadak; who have not come to you, distorting words from their places, being the people of Fadak, saying: If you are given this flogging, take it, and if you are not given it, beware of stoning."
"1328","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw myself last night as if a man fed me a lump of dates; I chewed it and found a date-stone in it which hurt me, so I spat it out. Then he fed me another lump, and the same, then another, and the same. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, let me interpret it. He said: Interpret it. He said: It is the army you sent; Allah will keep them safe and grant them spoils, then they will meet a man who will invoke your covenant of protection, so they will spare him; then they will meet another who will invoke your covenant of protection, so they will spare him; then they will meet another who will invoke your covenant of protection, so they will spare him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thus did the angel say, O Abu Bakr."
"1329","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: I heard Nubayh al-Anazi saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us from coming to women at night upon return from travel, then we came to them at night afterwards."
"1330","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: I heard Nubayh al-Anazi saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning the slain of Uhud that they be returned to their resting places, including those of them who had been carried away."
"1331","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you eat this green vegetable, do not sit with us in the gathering, for the angels are harmed by what people are harmed by."
"1332","Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Salih, who was better than his father, narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, who said: It was said to a man: Introduce yourself to us. He said: Your registrar is only the coarse, the miserly, the shabby, the grasping, the licking one, who when told: Here, take a bite, grabs, and when told: Give, withholds."
"1333","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: The Sunnah with us is that a man believe in the decree, its good and its evil, its sweet and its bitter, and that he know that what befell him was never going to miss him, and what missed him was never going to befall him, and that all of that is a decree from Allah, Mighty and Majestic. And that faith is word and deed, increasing and decreasing; no word benefits except with deed, and no deed and word except with intention, and no word and deed with intention except with adherence to the Sunnah. And invoking mercy upon all the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: And those who came after them say: Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith. We were commanded only with seeking forgiveness for them; whoever reviles them or belittles them or any one of them is not upon the Sunnah, and has no right in the fay. More than one informed us, from Malik ibn Anas, that he said: Allah, the Exalted, apportioned the fay and said: For the poor Muhajirun who were expelled from their homes, then He said: And those who came after them say: Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers, to the end of the verse. Whoever does not say this for them is not among those for whom the fay was appointed. And the Qur'an is the speech of Allah; I heard Sufyan saying: The Qur'an is the speech of Allah, and whoever says it is created is an innovator; we never heard anyone say this. And I heard Sufyan saying: Faith is word and deed, increasing and decreasing, whereupon his brother Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah said to him: O Abu Muhammad, do not say: Decreasing. He became angry and said: Be quiet, boy; indeed, even until nothing of it remains. And affirmation of the Vision after death, and of whatever the Qur'an and the hadith uttered, such as: And the Jews said: The hand of Allah is chained; chained are their hands, and such as: And the heavens folded in His right Hand, and whatever resembles this of the Qur'an and the hadith; we neither add to it nor interpret it; we stop where the Qur'an and the Sunnah stopped, and we say: The Most Merciful rose over the Throne. Whoever claims other than this is a negator, a Jahmi. And that one not say as the Khawarij said: Whoever commits a major sin has disbelieved. And we do not declare anyone a disbeliever for any sin; disbelief lies only in abandoning the five upon which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said Islam is built: Testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House. As for three of them, the one who abandons them is not to be debated: whoever does not testify, pray, or fast, for none of this is ever delayed beyond its time, and making it up after deliberately neglecting it beyond its time does not suffice. As for zakah, whenever one pays it, it suffices for him, though he was sinful in withholding it. As for Hajj, whoever is obligated with it and finds a way to it, it is obligatory upon him, yet it is not binding upon him in that very year such that he has no alternative; whenever he performs it, he has performed it, and he was not sinful in delaying it when he performed it, as he was sinful regarding zakah, for zakah is a right of poor Muslims which he withheld from them, so he was sinful until it reached them. As for Hajj, it was between him and his Lord; when he performed it, he has performed it, and if he dies while able and capable without having performed Hajj, he will ask to return to the world to perform Hajj, and his family must perform Hajj on his behalf, and we hope that suffices for him, just as if he had a debt which was paid on his behalf after his death."
